  "comments": "<p>The standard weight of these pieces was 48 to the pound or one third ounce avoirdupois (145.8 grains).<br><br>Due to the large number of pennies already circulating in 1953, these coins were not struck for circulation but were issued as part of the 9-coin Royal Mint set in a plastic envelope. It is thought that many of these sets were broken up with the coins ending up in circulation.<br><br>Also, a special proof set was released comprising 5s. to 1/4d. struck from polished dies and sold in special cases (40,000 issued).</p>",
